<applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI SHINTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASUGI SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MEGURO HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYATA KIYOYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, SHINTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASUGI, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MEGURO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYATA, KIYOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A cartridge body (4) storing a disk (5) of a disk cartridge is provided with a recording/reproducing opening and a central opening (25). Opposite inner surfaces of the cartridge body (4) are provided with liners (49, 51). The liners (49, 51) have contact portions and non-contact portions with respect to the cartridge body (4) and non-air-permeable layers are formed on the surface sides of the non-contact portions that face the cartridge body (4). The non-contact portions of the liners (49, 51) are allowed to float toward the disk (5) by an air stream generated by the rotation of the disk (5) until contacting the disk (5) to clean the disk.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un corps de cartouche (4) stockant un disque (5) de cartouche de disque, possédant une ouverture d'enregistrement/reproduction, et une ouverture centrale (25). Les surfaces intérieures opposées du corps de cartouche sont pourvues de doublures (49, 51). Ces doublures (49, 51) présentent des parties en contact avec le corps de cartouche (4) et des parties sans contact avec celui-ci. Des couches imperméables à l'air sont formées sur les surfaces des parties sans contact avec le corps de cartouche (4), opposées celui-ci. Les doublures (49, 51) des parties sans contact avec le corps de cartouche peuvent se diriger par flottement vers le disque (5), à l'aide d'un courant d'air produit par la rotation du disque (5), jusqu'à ce qu'elles viennent en contact avec ledit disque (5) afin de le nettoyer.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>